# kanagawa — Kanagawa (wave), dark.
#
# Upstream: https://github.com/rebelot/kanagawa.nvim
# Licence:  MIT
#
# Inspired by Hokusai's Great Wave, and the one palette here whose neutrals are
# not grey: sumiInk is a blue-black ink and fujiWhite a warm paper, so the
# ground carries a hue of its own rather than being a desaturated backdrop for
# the accents. That is what it contributes to this directory -- a warm-over-cool
# contrast none of the others have.

# -- neutrals: sumi ink, fuji white -----------------------------------------
COOL_BG0=#1F1F28          # sumiInk3
COOL_BG1=#2A2A37          # sumiInk4
COOL_BG2=#363646          # sumiInk5
COOL_FG0=#DCD7BA          # fujiWhite
COOL_FG1=#C8C093          # oldWhite
COOL_DIM=#938AA9          # springViolet1
COOL_DIMMER=#727169       # fujiGray
# -- the ramp: springBlue -> crystalBlue -> oniViolet -> sakura -> surimi ----
COOL_0=#7FB4CA
COOL_1=#7E9CD8
COOL_2=#957FB8
COOL_3=#D27E99
COOL_4=#FFA066
# -- alert pair -------------------------------------------------------------
COOL_HOT_0=#7FB4CA
COOL_HOT_4=#E82424        # samuraiRed
# -- off-ramp tints ---------------------------------------------------------
COOL_MINT=#98BB6C         # springGreen
COOL_BLUSH=#D27E99        # sakuraPink
# -- semantic aliases -------------------------------------------------------
COOL_ACCENT=#7E9CD8       # crystalBlue
COOL_ACTIVE=#957FB8       # oniViolet
COOL_URGENT=#FF5D62       # peachRed
COOL_WARN=#FF9E3B         # roninYellow
COOL_GOOD=#98BB6C         # springGreen
COOL_INACTIVE=#363646     # sumiInk5
